From: David Hamner <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.security.authentication.web.core: a work account signs in through the browser

Office's sign-in (OneAuth) asks the Web Account Manager for a token of
the person's work or school account. 0512 answered every provider
lookup with none, so Office fell back to its embedded sign-in page,
which goes white after the e-mail step under Wine's HTML engine.

A provider is found now (any id: it is a name), and its token requests
-- RequestTokenAsync, GetTokenSilentlyAsync and the with-account forms,
with the request's authority, client id, scopes, LoginHint and prompt
type -- are handed to sg-wam-msal (/usr/bin/sg-wam-msal, or the native
program SG_WAM_HELPER names), which asks Microsoft's own MSAL for the
token: the real sign-in page opens in the person's browser, the cache
answers later silent requests, and this code never sees a password. A
request the program cannot answer completes as for an account that is
not signed in (user interaction required; cancelled when the person
closes the page; a word like "cancelled" in any case says so). A
request for a given web account is for that account's token: its id and
user name go to the program. FindAllAccountsAsync lists the program's
accounts.

What Office's MSAL reads out of the answer is exact, and it throws the
whole sign-in away when a field is wrong:
 - the response property TokenExpiresOn is a decimal count of seconds
   since 1601 (it must exceed 11644473600; ISO and RFC 1123 dates and
   Unix seconds are refused, milliseconds and 100 ns ticks give a date
   out of range, and the token then counts as expired);
 - wamcompat_id_token, wamcompat_client_info and wamcompat_scopes
   accompany every answer, a cached one too ("Missing wamcompat_... in
   WAM case");
 - the web account's id is the MSAL home account id (uid.utid).
The interface definitions gain the token request, response and result
classes; Windows.Security.Credentials the web account's id and
properties and the provider's authority.

Gate: test/webauthcore-gate.sh, with a stub program
(test/webauthcore-helper.sh): provider lookups, an interactive and a
silent request, the answer's properties, cancel and the login hint.
Mutants: SG_MUTANT_WAM_NO_EXPIRES_ON, SG_MUTANT_WAM_NO_WAMCOMPAT.
